You implement a money transfer inside one JDBC transaction. The audit insert fails, but you forgot to roll back. What is the final state after this method returns?

```java
void transfer(DataSource ds, long fromId, long toId, BigDecimal amount) throws SQLException {
    try (Connection c = ds.getConnection()) {
        c.setAutoCommit(false);
        try {
            try (PreparedStatement ps = c.prepareStatement(
                    "UPDATE account SET balance = balance - ? WHERE id = ?")) {
                ps.setBigDecimal(1, amount);
                ps.setLong(2, fromId);
                ps.executeUpdate();
            }
            try (PreparedStatement ps = c.prepareStatement(
                    "UPDATE account SET balance = balance + ? WHERE id = ?")) {
                ps.setBigDecimal(1, amount);
                ps.setLong(2, toId);
                ps.executeUpdate();
            }
            // This fails due to FK violation (bug in audit reference)
            try (PreparedStatement ps = c.prepareStatement(
                    "INSERT INTO transfer_audit(tx_id, from_id, to_id, amount) VALUES(?,?,?,?)")) {
                ps.setLong(1, 9999L); // bad fk
                ps.setLong(2, fromId);
                ps.setLong(3, toId);
                ps.setBigDecimal(4, amount);
                ps.executeUpdate();
            }
            c.commit();
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            // forgot: no rollback here
            // log and continue
        }
        c.commit(); // second commit
    }
}
```

